+## Sales and variance
+
+`POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the header
+`ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` an ISO instant, `qty` a whole number).
+Each line uses `qty` portions of the dish's recipe (ledger ref
+`sale:<ticket>`). Tickets already imported are skipped. The answer is
+`{ "tickets": <new tickets>, "dishes": <portions sold> }`. A bad row is
+`bad_request` and an item running out is `sale_out_of_stock` (409); both
+name the row (`row 2` is the first data row) and nothing is imported.
+
+`GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists, per item with
+any use, `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }`:
+theoretical use from sales sold in those days (inclusive), actual use from
+every `consume` movement in those days, and `difference = actual -
+theoretical`.
